course: dictionary
lesson: 10587
title: Undergrowth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Undergrowth is the low, tangled plants that grow under the trees in a wood or forest: bushes, ferns, small plants and thin stems. Look at the word itself. Under means below, and growth means things growing, so undergrowth is the growing things under the trees.
explain: «Hotter, drier years make bushfire seasons longer and fiercer, scientists said, and fire experts say clearing dry undergrowth matters too.» The clues are dry, fire and clearing. Dry plants under the trees are the kind that can catch fire, so undergrowth must mean the low plants on the forest floor.
explain: Stories use the undergrowth too. When something rustles in the undergrowth, the writer wants you to wonder what is hiding there. Try the swap check: put «the low plants under the trees» in place of undergrowth, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Undergrowth means bushes, ferns, small plants and tangled stems that grow under the trees in a wood or forest.
fact: Undergrowth is uncountable, so say «some undergrowth», not «an undergrowth» or «undergrowths».
fact: «Thick undergrowth» means many tangled plants, which can be hard to push through.
fact: In science, the undergrowth is a habitat: insects, birds and mice can live there.
fact: In stories, «rustling in the undergrowth» often suggests that something is hiding there.
exercise: «The path disappeared into thick undergrowth.» What does undergrowth mean here? | *Bushes, ferns and tangled small plants under the trees | The tall trees high above the path | The stones on the ground | A grey, wet sky
exercise: Fire experts say clearing dry undergrowth matters too. What is the undergrowth in that sentence? | *Dry bushes and plants growing under the trees | Fire engines on the road | The hottest months of the year | Rain clouds over the hills
exercise: In a story, a rustle in the undergrowth makes the reader think what? | *Something might be hiding there | The wind is blowing the sea | The sun has come out | The children are having lunch
test: Which sentence uses undergrowth correctly? | Undergrowth was run very fast. | *The deer hid in the thick undergrowth. | We saw an undergrowth. | The undergrowths are a wood.
test: What does undergrowth mean? | A river with fish in it | *Small plants, bushes and ferns growing under the trees | The very top branches of the tallest trees | A path made of stones
exam: Scientists say the undergrowth of a forest is home to which animals? | Whales and sharks | Penguins on the ice | *Insects, birds and mice | Camels crossing the desert
